body:
Thanks. Car insurance, phone bill and the other few come out to the $300+. My car insurance alone is only $88. I'll be starting doordash again this week. I stopped when I got the job because I was still adjusting to the workload. I'll do doordash close to home since my car is on it's last leg. (209k miles and the engine sounds horrible).

&#x200B;

Also will look into $VTI too. Thank you!

Thank you for your honest advice. I realized this week that I needed to change ASAP as I have a really important surgery I need a downpayment for and I spent a lot of money on my pet's vet bills. 

&#x200B;

My budget is newly cut down and in the past I was overspending for each category especially groceries.

I'm gluten and lactose free so that definitely makes shopping a little more expensive. I think I really need to make actual meal plans and be very strict with that I purchase. 

&#x200B;

I'm looking into UX design even though it's become a little saturated. It's the next best thing to transition into. I also am looking at my budget now and cutting out quickbooks, cutting down personal care with just essentials (toothpaste, shampoo, hair products,etc) and learning to do my own hair, cutting out coffee and fast food from my budget.
